From: buntOS contributors
Subject: [PATCH] clk: mediatek: add the MT6897 display clock gates

Add the dispsys0, dispsys1, ovlsys0, ovlsys1 and mminfra blocks of MT6897,
with the registers and bits of the MediaTek driver in the OnePlus MT6897
kernel (clk-mt6897-mmsys.c). The same module of the stock firmware of the
Lenovo TB375FC has the same tables. Part of the gates go through the
hardware voter. As in the vendor tables, the gates of dispsys1 and ovlsys1
have the disp0 and ovl0 muxes as their parents.

The bootloader leaves the display running on these blocks, and probing
touches neither the registers nor the power domains. The gates have no
status read, so the clock core leaves them alone until a consumer enables
them.

The MT8196 display clock drivers are written to be children of mtk-mmsys,
but mtk-mmsys has no data for either SoC yet. So these blocks bind by
compatible for now. They move to mtk-mmsys with the display pipeline.

---
 drivers/clk/mediatek/Kconfig            |  10 +
 drivers/clk/mediatek/Makefile           |   1 +
 drivers/clk/mediatek/clk-mt6897-mmsys.c | 395 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 406 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/mediatek/Kconfig b/drivers/clk/mediatek/Kconfig
index 82fb6380c..f538cdd24 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/mediatek/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/clk/mediatek/Kconfig
@@ -395,6 +395,16 @@ config COMMON_CLK_MT6897_IMP_IIC_WRAP
 	  clock from one of these gates. Say Y or M here when a device on the
 	  I2C buses is used.
 
+config COMMON_CLK_MT6897_MMSYS
+	tristate "Clock driver for MediaTek MT6897 mmsys"
+	depends on COMMON_CLK_MT6897
+	default COMMON_CLK_MT6897
+	help
+	  This driver supports the MediaTek MT6897 clock gates of the display
+	  blocks (dispsys0, dispsys1, ovlsys0, ovlsys1) and of mminfra. Part of
+	  the gates are switched through the hardware voter. Say Y or M here
+	  when the display pipeline is used.
+
 config COMMON_CLK_MT6897_UFSSYS
 	tristate "Clock driver for MediaTek MT6897 ufssys"
 	depends on COMMON_CLK_MT6897
diff --git a/drivers/clk/mediatek/Makefile b/drivers/clk/mediatek/Makefile
index a978375a7..1f4c9a1d3 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/mediatek/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/clk/mediatek/Makefile
@@ -37,6 +37,7 @@ obj-$(CONFIG_COMMON_CLK_MT6797_VENCSYS) += clk-mt6797-venc.o
